{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 27]], "date-time": "2026-09-27T12:00:14Z", "timestamp": 1790510414025, "version": "4.1.0"}, "reference-count": 45, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "4", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2017, 6, 13]], "date-time": "2017-06-13T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1497312000000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/termsAndConditions#vor"}], "funder": [{"name": "Danish Research Counsil"}, {"name": "Pajbjerg Foundation"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Plant Breeding"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2017, 8]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title><jats:p>Fungal diseases are a major constraint for wheat production. Effective disease resistance is essential for ensuring a high production quality and yield. One of the most severe fungal diseases of wheat is Septoria tritici blotch (<jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">STB</jats:styled-content>), which influences wheat production across the world. In this study, genomewide association mapping was used to identify new chromosomal regions on the wheat genome conferring effective resistance towards <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">STB</jats:styled-content>. A winter wheat population of 164 North European varieties and breeding lines was genotyped with 15K single nucleotide polymorphism (<jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">SNP</jats:styled-content>) wheat array. The varieties were evaluated for <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">STB</jats:styled-content> in field trials at three locations in Denmark and across 3\u00a0years. The association analysis revealed four quantitative trait loci, on chromosomes 1B, 2A, 5D and 7A, highly associated with <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">STB</jats:styled-content> resistance. By comparing varieties containing several quantitative trait loci (<jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">QTL</jats:styled-content>) with varieties containing none of the found <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">QTL</jats:styled-content>, a significant difference was found in the mean disease score. This indicates that an effective resistance can be obtained by pyramiding several <jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\">QTL</jats:styled-content>.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1111/pbr.12490", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2017, 6, 14]], "date-time": "2017-06-14T02:42:38Z", "timestamp": 1497408158000}, "page": "474-482", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 35, "title": ["Genomewide association study reveals novel quantitative trait loci associated with resistance towards Septoria tritici blotch in North European winter wheat"], "prefix": "10.1111", "volume": "136", "author": [{"given": "Nana", "family": "Vagndorf", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Nordic Seed A/S Odder Denmark"}, {"name": "Department of Agroecology Flakkebjerg Research Centre Aarhus University Slagelse Denmark"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Nanna Hellum", "family": "Nielsen", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Nordic Seed A/S Odder Denmark"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Vahid", "family": "Edriss", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Nordic Seed A/S Odder Denmark"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Jeppe Reitan", "family": "Andersen", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Nordic Seed A/S Odder Denmark"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9641-6657", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Jihad", "family": "Orabi", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Nordic Seed A/S Odder Denmark"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Lise Nistrup", "family": "J\u00f8rgensen", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Agroecology Flakkebjerg Research Centre Aarhus University Slagelse Denmark"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Ahmed", "family": "Jahoor", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Nordic Seed A/S Odder Denmark"}, {"name": "Department of Plant Breeding The Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences Alnarp Sweden"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "311", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2017, 6, 13]]}, "reference": [{"key": "e_1_2_6_2_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.2135/cropsci2004.1403"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_3_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.5539/jmbr.v1n1p20"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_4_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1094/PHYTO.2002.92.4.439"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_5_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/j.fgb.2015.04.017"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_6_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s11032-008-9210-6"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_7_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1111/j.1365-3059.2004.01052.x"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_8_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s00122-005-1945-4"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_9_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1002/ps.1568"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_10_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1046/j.1365-3059.2000.00472.x"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_11_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s00122-015-2587-9"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_12_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s00122-003-1276-2"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_13_1", "volume-title": "The Septoria diseases of wheat: Concepts and methods of disease management", "author": "Eyal Z.", "year": "1987"}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_14_1", "unstructured": "Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations (FAO). Crop statistics. Retrieved fromhttp://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QC/visualize."}, {"key": "e_1_2_6_15_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s00122-011-1692-7"}, {"key": "e_1_2_